{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 progress — RED->GREEN evidence (measurement run still in flight)\n\n**Gerrit change:** not yet pushed — pushing before the measurement lands would guarantee a\n`Verified -1`, because the budget-vs-measurement cell is deliberately RED until\n`MEASURED_FIELD_REGISTRATION_S` is filled from the run.\n\n**Plan review:** PASS, 0 blocking, 4 advisory, attestation certified. Two advisories were\nworth acting on and both are addressed:\n- the bootstrap-circularity finding (E6/E2 + G6) — resolved in practice: the dispatched run\n  carries BOTH the raised budget AND the new success line, so one run harvests the\n  measurement and verifies the fix.\n- the 2x-provenance finding (G6) — corrected. The 316s/485s figures are stage-ONE\n  (`serverInfo`) durations, NOT stage-two field registration. The code comment, the test\n  docstring and the README now say so explicitly and label the multiplier a runner-variance\n  PROXY to be retired once a second green run supplies a real stage-two spread.\n\n**RED proof (against pre-fix source checked out from origin/main, fix absent):**\n- `test_the_field_budget_covers_the_measured_registration_time` — AttributeError: module\n  `jira_dc_field_readiness` has no attribute `MEASURED_FIELD_REGISTRATION_S`\n- `test_a_successful_wait_records_how_long_registration_took` — 'a successful field wait\n  recorded nothing ... captured stdout was ``''``'\n- `test_a_degraded_image_with_other_custom_fields_still_fails_loudly` — PASSED pre-fix. Stated\n  honestly: it is a REGRESSION PIN for AC3, not a RED oracle. Its job is to stop the raised\n  budget from becoming a longer silence, and its teeth are proven by mutation below.\n\n**Mutation checks (fix perturbed, tests must return to RED):**\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `await_required_fields` returns `ready=True` on expiry (the exact 9790 blindness) | 3 cells RED incl. the degrade cell — DID NOT RAISE RuntimeError |\n| degrade-branch prose dropped from `not_ready_message` | degrade cell RED |\n| the conftest success `print` removed | measurement cell RED |\nFix restored byte-identical afterwards (`diff` clean).\n\n**Gates:** `make lint` exit **0**, `make typecheck` exit **0** (434 files).\nCI marker selection `pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -n 4 --dist worksteal -q`:\n2 failed / 10291 passed / 46 skipped. One failure is the intentional pending-measurement cell.\nThe other, `tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py::test_full_backend_account_is_present`,\nis **pre-existing on origin/main** — reproduced on a clean worktree detached at d68907dbe2 with\nnone of this change present — and is filed as [rebar:78f4-8cc7-bc8c-4ac2], linked\n`discovered_from` this bug.\n\n**Capture check:** verified that a session-autouse fixture's `print` survives the job's exact\n`pytest -q -rA` flags, so the measurement will actually reach the log rather than being\nswallowed — checked before spending the run, not after."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785909592490460001,"uuid":"ef9c0fdb-1994-4375-b5f6-ea6117f3a82f"}